<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106805" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπᾴδω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sing by way of accompaniment,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λίνον δ᾽ ὑπὸ καλὸν ἄειδε</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ φόρμιγγι</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.570
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ δ᾽ ὑπὸ καλὸν ἄεισε</span>
			(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ νευρή</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				21.411
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς Μούσαις τι μέλος ὑπᾴσατε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					874
				</span></i>
			; without acc., <i>to accompany with the voice,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χοροῖσι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				366
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Salt.</u>
				30
			</span></i>; in poet. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπαείδω</span></b> , aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπήεισαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Dian.</u>
					242
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. νόμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Del.</u>
					304
				</span></i>
			. [The a of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπαείδω</span> used
			long by <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
			</span></i> l. c.]</div>
